      "problem": "Given that ${n}^{2}+24n+144=0,$ what are the values of $n?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the left-hand side is a perfect square. It just needs to be factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+24n+144 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2}+2\\cdot 12\\cdot n+{12}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (n+12)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(n+12)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |n+12| & =0 \\\\ n+12 & =0 \\\\ n & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
